  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming Seaweed Farming for Enhanced Food Systems in Zanzibar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 2028, an estimated 15,000 seaweed-farming households in Kaskazini Unguja and Kaskazini Pemba, Zanzibar, are expected to achieve a 40 per cent increase in income through the transformation of seaweed farming from a subsistence activity into a dynamic and sustainable economic sector. This transformation will be enabled by integrated and closely coordinated United Nations support and driven by integrated financial solutions, value addition strategies, cooperative development and improved access</narrative>
  </description>
